.TH PORTFWD 1 "2026-09" "port-forward-manager" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
portfwd \- run several kubectl port-forwards from a profile, with auto-reconnect
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B portfwd
.I command
.RI [ profile | name ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Starts and supervises several
.B kubectl port-forward
processes described in one profile file, reconnecting each one when it
drops \(em which is what a hand-run port-forward does not do.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR up " [\fIprofile\fR] [\fB\-\-reason\fR \fITEXT\fR]"
Start every forward in the profile. The default profile is
.I ./portfwd.yaml
or
.IR ~/.config/portfwd/default.yaml .
If any forward in the profile is protected,
.B \-\-reason
is required and the whole run is refused without it; see
.BR "PROTECTED FORWARDS" .
.TP
.BR env " [\fIprofile\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR \fIdotenv\fR|\fIexport\fR|\fIjson\fR]"
Print the profile as environment variables, two per forward:
.IB NAME _HOST
(always
.BR localhost )
and
.IB NAME _PORT
(the local half of
.BR ports ).
.I NAME
is the forward's
.B name
uppercased, with every character that is not a letter or a digit replaced by
an underscore. The default format is
.IR dotenv .
.TP
.B status
Show the forwards and their health. A protected forward is marked
.BR [protected] .
.TP
.BI logs " NAME"
Tail one forward's log.
.TP
.B down
Stop everything.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ./portfwd.yaml
Default profile: a
.B forwards:
list, one block per forward, each with
.BR name ,
.BR target ,
.B ports
and optionally
.BR namespace ,
.B context
and
.BR protected .
An optional
.B contexts:
list marks whole contexts
.BR protected .
.TP
.I ~/.config/portfwd/default.yaml
Fallback profile when there is none in the working directory.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/portfwd/protected.log
One tab-separated line per finished protected session: context, namespace,
target, user, start, end, reason. Created mode 0600. Override with
.BR PORTFWD_AUDIT_LOG .
.SH PROTECTED FORWARDS
A forward with
.B protected: true
\(em or one whose
.B context
is listed under
.B contexts:
with
.B protected: true
\(em cannot be opened without
.BR "\-\-reason \fITEXT\fR" .
The run is refused whole rather than in part, so a profile that names
production is opened deliberately or not at all. When the session ends,
.B portfwd down
appends the record to the log above. A session cut short with the machine is
closed out with
.B interrupted
as its end on the next
.BR "portfwd up" .
There is no server and no privileged helper: the log is a local file.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PORTFWD_STATE_DIR
Where per-forward pid, log and state files live. Default
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/portfwd-$USER .
.TP
.B PORTFWD_RECONNECT_DELAY
Seconds to wait before reconnecting a dropped forward. Default 2.
.TP
.B PORTFWD_AUDIT_LOG
Where finished protected sessions are appended. Default
.IR $XDG_STATE_HOME/portfwd/protected.log .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command completed.
.TP
.B 64
.BR portfwd (1)
was invoked wrong: no profile, an unknown option, or an unknown
.BR \-\-format .
.TP
.B 77
A protected forward was opened without
.BR \-\-reason .
.TP
.B non-zero
The profile was missing or invalid, or a forward could not be started.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Bring up every forward in the local profile:
.PP
.RS
.B portfwd up
.RE
.PP
See what is connected:
.PP
.RS
.B portfwd status
.RE
.PP
Follow one of them:
.PP
.RS
.B portfwd logs db
.RE
.PP
Write the project's
.I .env
from the same profile:
.PP
.RS
.B portfwd env > .env
.RE
.PP
Open a protected forward, on the record:
.PP
.RS
.B portfwd up \-\-reason \(dqINC-4711: replaying the stuck batch\(dq
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kubectl (1).
Project documentation:
https://github.com/fabiocicerchia/port-forward-manager
